{"name":"One Dozen","hex":"#65362e","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"one","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["NATO & ICAO radiotelephony clear code (spelling-alphabet name) for the digit 1."]},{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Oneida."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/one"},{"term":"dozen","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A set of twelve.","A large, unspecified number of, comfortably estimated in small multiples of twelve, thus generally implied to be significantly more than ten or twelve, but less than perhaps one or two hundred; many."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A member of a K-pop group who has no talent."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dozen"}],"entries":[{"title":"1","blocks":[{"text":"1 is a number, numeral, and grapheme. It is the first and smallest positive integer of the infinite sequence of natural numbers. This fundamental property has led to its unique uses in other fields, ranging from science to sports, where it commonly denotes the first, leading, or top thing in a group. 1 is the unit of counting or measurement, and represents a single thing. The representation of 1 evolved from ancient Sumerian and Babylonian symbols to the modern Arabic numeral. Linguistically, in English, \"one\" is a determiner for singular nouns and a gender-neutral pronoun."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1"},{"title":"Dozen","blocks":[{"text":"A dozen is a grouping of twelve."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/82/Box_of_Duck_Donuts_1.jpg/330px-Box_of_Duck_Donuts_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dozen"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b6/Woodstock_typewriter%2C_1940s%2C_daylight_-_keyboard.jpg/500px-Woodstock_typewriter%2C_1940s%2C_daylight_-_keyboard.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&u